      "finding_id": "queue-base-guard",
      "issue_key": "CultureBotAI/CMMMech:round63-queue-admission-base-guard",
      "severity": "major",
      "priority": "P2",
      "status": "resolved",
      "target": "/private/tmp/cmm-round63-enqueue.py",
      "reviewed_sha256": "2371cec932c85cf48a51d72ddd3b0530efc5edb1d9e8d88b95b087ead34c1dbf",
      "description": "The queue helper checks the topic head and stored preflight head/tree but does not verify preflight mode/trusted_base or fresh remote main against the reviewed base immediately before admission. A main advance after preflight can be admitted; later cleanup and hosted audit detect parent/tree mismatch only after merge.",
      "correction": "Require mode=preflight, trusted_base equal commit receipt base, matching successful commands/log and a fresh read-only remote main/base equality observation immediately before enqueue; retain that observation in the queue receipt. A subsequent concurrent update remains a native queue race.",
      "acceptance": "Inspect revised guard, compile helper, exercise the guard in an isolated mocked command harness with matching and changed base and mismatched preflight identity; no live enqueue required for this regression.",
      "disposition_reason": "Actual guard functions now check full preflight identity/evidence and live main immediately before admission; maintained profile updated; all 14 isolated regression cases passed and both independent reviewers verified source/receipt hashes.",
